  "notes": "The one entry on this axis with real harmony. The 2022 record's stated inputs are \"traditional hip-hop, drum and bass, trap, poetry, and jazz\", and the research says that shows up as m7/m9 extensions and modal jazz voicings replacing bare triads — so `extensions.seventh` and `ninth` are roughly triple the parent's, `maxChords` is 4, and `ii–v–i` sits in the family list next to the hard-cut `i–VI–VII`. The drums move the other way: `kick.densityPerBar` and `syncopation` are the highest in this batch (\"kick dense and syncopated with 16th pickups\"), and `snare.layerClapOffsetMs` is 0–2ms with `bass808.clipping` on because the Ronny J productions run the whole drum bus into clipping until the kick and clap fuse. The countermelody is authored up rather than down — the research names siren/whistle counter-lines as tension devices, which is a part, not a texture. `modes` are the documented Light / Gray / Dark act structure the research explicitly suggests the engine mirror as a three-part intensity ramp; the Light mode is the only place in this batch that turns `halfTime` off, because the jazz/drum-and-bass-facing cuts are described as 165–175 straight. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it high-medium and marks the 165–175 figure `[LOW-CONF]`: the whole tempo span is the inferred parameter. ⚠ `dorian` in the scale bank is INFERRED — the research says \"modal jazz voicings\" without naming a mode; it carries the lowest weight.",
